        {
          "sid": "family-t1-s01",
          "c": "我爸爸好高。",
          "j": "ngo5 baa4 baa1 hou2 gou1.",
          "e": "My father is very tall.",
          "note": "With close family you can drop the 嘅 (ge3) \"'s\" — 我爸爸 (ngo5 baa4 baa1) \"my dad\", not 我嘅爸爸 (ngo5 ge3 baa4 baa1). Note the tone shift in doubled kinship words: 爸爸 (baa4 baa1), the second syllable lifting high — same in 媽媽 (maa4 maa1), 哥哥 (go4 go1).",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "my"
            },
            {
              "c": "爸爸",
              "j": "baa4 baa1",
              "e": "father"
            },
            {
              "c": "好高",
              "j": "hou2 gou1",
              "e": "very tall"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "family-t1-s02",
          "c": "我媽媽係老師。",
          "j": "ngo5 maa4 maa1 hai6 lou5 si1.",
          "e": "My mother is a teacher.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "my"
            },
            {
              "c": "媽媽",
              "j": "maa4 maa1",
              "e": "mother"
            },
            {
              "c": "係",
              "j": "hai6",
              "e": "is"
            },
            {
              "c": "老師",
              "j": "lou5 si1",
              "e": "teacher"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "family-t1-s03",
          "c": "我有一個哥哥。",
          "j": "ngo5 jau5 jat1 go3 go4 go1.",
          "e": "I have one older brother.",
          "note": "Cantonese names siblings by age, not just gender — 哥哥 (go4 go1) \"older brother\", 弟弟 (dai4 dai2) \"younger brother\", 姐姐 (ze4 ze1) \"older sister\", 妹妹 (mui4 mui2) \"younger sister\". There's no single word for just \"brother\"; you must pick older or younger.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我",
              "j": "ngo5",
              "e": "I"
            },
            {
              "c": "有",
              "j": "jau5",
              "e": "have"
            },
            {
              "c": "一個",
              "j": "jat1 go3",
              "e": "one (person)"
            },
            {
              "c": "哥哥",
              "j": "go4 go1",
              "e": "older brother"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "family-t1-s04",
          "c": "妹妹好細個。",
          "j": "mui4 mui2 hou2 sai3 go3.",
          "e": "Younger sister is very young.",
          "note": "細 (sai3) is the Cantonese \"small\" (Mandarin 小 (siu2)), and 細個 (sai3 go3) means \"young / little\" of a person — 好細個 (hou2 sai3 go3) \"very young\". Its opposite is 大 (daai6) \"big / grown / older\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "妹妹",
              "j": "mui4 mui2",
              "e": "younger sister"
            },
            {
              "c": "好",
              "j": "hou2",
              "e": "very"
            },
            {
              "c": "細個",
              "j": "sai3 go3",
              "e": "young / small"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "family-t1-s05",
          "c": "爺爺住喺香港。",
          "j": "je4 je2 zyu6 hai2 hoeng1 gong2.",
          "e": "Grandfather lives in Hong Kong.",
          "note": "Grandparents split by side of the family: 爺爺 (je4 je2) and 嫲嫲 (maa4 maa4) are your father's parents; 公公 (gung4 gung1) and 婆婆 (po4 po2) are your mother's. 住喺 (zyu6 hai2) is \"live at\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "爺爺",
              "j": "je4 je2",
              "e": "paternal grandfather"
            },
            {
              "c": "住",
              "j": "zyu6",
              "e": "lives"
            },
            {
              "c": "喺",
              "j": "hai2",
              "e": "in / at"
            },
            {
              "c": "香港",
              "j": "hoeng1 gong2",
              "e": "Hong Kong"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "family-t1-s06",
          "c": "嫲嫲今年八十歲。",
          "j": "maa4 maa4 gam1 nin4 baat3 sap6 seoi3.",
          "e": "Grandma is eighty this year.",
          "note": "To give an age, say the number then <strong>歲</strong> (seoi3) \"years old\" — 八十歲 (baat3 sap6 seoi3) \"eighty\". No word for \"is\" is needed.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "嫲嫲",
              "j": "maa4 maa4",
              "e": "grandma (father's mother)"
            },
            {
              "c": "今年",
              "j": "gam1 nin4",
              "e": "this year"
            },
            {
              "c": "八十歲",
              "j": "baat3 sap6 seoi3",
              "e": "eighty years old"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
